          "start_line": 1133
        }
      ],
      "key": "iacs_derivation_and_closure",
      "statement": "Derive IACS from accepted Ontology before naming subordinate payloads/modules; the set should precede helper results/internal detail. Possible roles include source truth, admission, execution, yield/recovery, effect plan and public projection, not a fixed required inventory. Branch payload, persistence detail, read-row shape and typing-only field grouping do not automatically justify top-level carriers. Evidence cites accepted Ontology/function derivation, declares set, maps every carrier to carried identity/lifecycle/function/authority/effect/projection law, distinguishes authoritative/downstream carriers, defaults all other shapes to subordinate/private unless Promotion Test passes, and reconciles typed implementation before closure. IACS cannot replace Ontology or originate entities/functions/lifecycle/authority. Missing declared accepted Ontology or IACS means schema not yet design-method complete. Before promotion/closure both must be accepted and implementation reconciled; gated mode accepts affected unresolved/contradictory/non-equivalent relation before retained implementation establishes it.",
